			<div class="content" id="post-content-2265247">
									

<p>Okay, I've tried to punch it up a bit, hint more as to what is happening, and create a stronger narrative both in the cult portion (trying to attract the attention of the phantom surgeons) and the Foundation angle (this SCP was quickly written off as fairly harmless and thus has fallen through the cracks despite having serious implications, playing on the increasingly massive list of ever-more worldthreatening and intensively wrangled SCPs we have on the list).</p>
<p>This one is a bit of a balancing act. If I hint in the document too strongly that something is up, it becomes unbelievable that the Foundation would like this slip by. If it is too subtle, it just becomes crazypaint. I hope this is a more workable balance.</p>

